    "result_text": "The test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"the money I am owed should only count invoices I have actually sent; don't count drafts\" \u2014 was a single-line correctness fix on the server.\n\n**Root cause:** The dashboard's outstanding total summed invoices `WHERE status = 'UNPAID'`, a legacy status value that no longer fits the invoice lifecycle. The lifecycle (per `V8` migration and `SendInvoice`/`PayInvoice`) is `DRAFT \u2192 SENT \u2192 PAID`, so nothing is ever `'UNPAID'` anymore \u2014 and that query would silently include or exclude the wrong rows.\n\n**Fix:** `src/main/java/.../dashboard/GetDashboard.java` now sums `WHERE status = 'SENT'` \u2014 invoices that have been sent but not yet paid. Drafts (not yet sent) and paid invoices are correctly excluded.\n\nNo schema migration or front-end change was needed: the `status` column already exists, the `/__test__` seed already supports it, and the `dashboard-outstanding-total` testid was already wired. With the test fixture (100 SENT + 200 SENT + 50 DRAFT + 30 PAID), the total is now `$300.00` and the test passes.",
